  data: {
    LLM: "Avoid the Ace. In Badeucy, the Ace is a 'dead card' for your low hand. If you start with an Ace, discard it immediately unless it's part of a desperate Badugi bluff.\n\nManage suits carefully. Unlike Badacey where flushes don't matter, in Badeucy you must ACTIVELY AVOID flushes for your Lowball half. This means your 4-card Badugi (mixed suits) is naturally aligned with a good Lowball hand.\n\nRange Polarization: Because straights and flushes are 'bad', you can tell a lot about an opponent's hand by how many cards they draw. Specifically, a player drawing zero cards ('Standing Pat') is very likely to have a 7-low or 8-low that is NOT a straight.",
    Player: "Avoid the Ace. In Badeucy, the Ace is a 'dead card' for your low hand. If you start with an Ace, discard it immediately unless it's part of a desperate Badugi bluff.\n\nManage suits carefully. Unlike Badacey where flushes don't matter, in Badeucy you must ACTIVELY AVOID flushes for your Lowball half. This means your 4-card Badugi (mixed suits) is naturally aligned with a good Lowball hand.\n\nRange Polarization: Because straights and flushes are 'bad', you can tell a lot about an opponent's hand by how many cards they draw. Specifically, a player drawing zero cards ('Standing Pat') is very likely to have a 7-low or 8-low that is NOT a straight.",
